-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/32e55f36-8fec-58b9-b6dd-f6f43d9d269e
-- title:
--   Smooth Igusa base model off the supersingular locus, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime assumed equal to $2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa$ for `ResidueField A`. Three fields of Laurent series enter: `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by `jqModC κ` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field; and $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` denotes the resulting inclusion.
--
--   The data are: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is the places $w$ that are rational (the map $\kappa \to$ $w$'s residue field is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen κ M'` in the set `ssJSet q κ`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue map onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal and agreeing with the residue map of $A$ on constants, together with the scaling axiom, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisor push-forward of principal divisors), subject to the coefficientwise compatibility `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (an element of `Idx q`); families $O^{\mathrm{Ig}} =$ `OIg` of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb{Z}/q$, and $O^{\mathrm{ss}} =$ `OSS` of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa pins are four hypotheses. `hIg_inf` presents $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, at the line $[1:0]$, as a Gauss ring: $f$ belongs to it if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. `hIg` asserts that every line $\ell$ is of the form `redQ q γ • lineInfty q` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. `hIg_inj` says $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective, and `hIg_perm` that for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   The supersingular (Drinfeld) pins are four hypotheses. `hSS_A` says that for each $s \in W$ a constant lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ precisely when it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` says: for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$. `hSS_fix` says each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   Further: a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring `R.integers` with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with the scaling axiom), with `hR` identifying `R.integers` with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and `hR₀O` identifying `R₀.integers` with the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ under the inclusion. A tame element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$.
--
--   The small-constants data consist of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field, together with the approximation hypothesis `hκ`: every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Next, an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally one finite layer of constants: an intermediate field $K_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, finite over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ which is cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`), and is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $F$ obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$. It asserts the existence of an intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$, a finite set $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa$, and, indexed by all such places $Q$, a subring $S_Q$ of $F$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q : A_1[X] \to S_Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa$ and a set $D_Q$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that the following hold.
--
--   (1) The $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $F$.
--
--   (2) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   (3) $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and $W$ have the same cardinality.
--
--   (4) There is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` such that: for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue is $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$; and $Q \in N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds if and only if there is $s \in W$ with the property that a function $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ exactly when $j(g)$ lies in that of $Q$.
--
--   (5) Every valuation subring of $F$ that contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and is not all of $F$ is a principal ideal ring.
--
--   (6) Linear disjointness of the constants from $F_0$: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$, and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ with all $a_i$ in the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$ together with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   (7) For every place $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$: the map sending $a \in A_1$ to the residue in $\kappa$ of its image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is surjective; the image in $F$ of every $a \in A_1$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(\mathrm{C}\,a)$ is that image; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(\mathrm{C}\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; $S_Q$ carries a local ring structure whose maximal ideal is the kernel of $\chi_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_Q$ is contained in the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$ together with $F_0$, and conversely every element $f$ of that subfield satisfies $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_Q$ with $h \neq 0$; every element of $S_Q$ lies in `R.integers`, and for every uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A_1$ an element $f \in S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` if and only if $\varphi_Q(\mathrm{C}\,\varpi)$ divides $f$ in $S_Q$; for every $f \in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q$'s residue field; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; and $D_Q$ consists exactly of the places $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that are rational, for which every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for which, for every $f \in S_Q$, the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$.
--
--   (8) The discs separate the places: if $Q, Q' \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and some $P$ lies in $D_Q$ and in $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$.
--
--   (9) Equivariance under the group generated by the level automorphisms: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of $F$ generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ` of the reduced field satisfies: $Q$ lies in $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ if and only if its translate does, and for $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ the translated disc `smulDisc τ (D Q)`, namely $\{P \mid \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_Q\}$, equals $D$ at the translate of $Q$.
--
--   (10) Inertia invariance: for every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` that preserves $K_1$, and every $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, an element $f$ of $F$ lies in $S_Q$ if and only if its image under the coefficientwise arithmetic action [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) does, and $\chi_Q$ takes the same value on $f$ and on that image.
--
--   (11) For every $g$ in the same subgroup generated by the level automorphisms whose pullback moves $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and for all $Q, Q' \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$: if $P \in D_Q$ then $g \cdot P \notin D_{Q'}$.
--
--   (12) The discs avoid the supersingular tubes: for $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, $P \in D_Q$ and $s \in W$, it is not the case that both of the following hold — the image in $F$ of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen κ M'` the difference of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; and the same two conditions for the image of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (qExpand ℚ M' jq)` with `jNGeomGen κ M'` in place of `jGeomGen κ M'`.
--
--   (13) Conversely, every place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is not centred at any supersingular place — that is, for which no $s \in W$ has the property that for all $f \in$ `R₀.integers` with non-negative order at every place where `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` has non-negative order and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and all $a \in A$ whose residue is $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ — admits $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a place $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ • P` $\in D_Q$.
--
--   (14) There is a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose valuation subring is `qIntegersBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')`, the ring of elements of non-negative Laurent order, and a place $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with $P \in D_Q$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the construction, over one finite layer $K_1$ of constants, of an integral model of the Igusa-type covering attached to $X_{\Gamma_H(q^2M')}$ which is smooth away from a finite set $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places matching the supersingular locus $W$ of level $M'$, each smooth stalk being presented by an étale coordinate $\varphi_Q : A_1[X] \to S_Q$ with a residue character $\chi_Q$ and a residue disc $D_Q$, equivariantly for the level automorphisms and for inertia. It feeds the assembly of the Igusa tower data in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaTower_smoothPointData_of_stable_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaTower_smoothPointData_of_stable_of_eq_two), on the semistable-covering leg of the level-lowering argument.
